<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine crops helped by rain - traders.</title>
<headline>Argentine crops helped by rain - traders.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's developing maize, sunflower and soybean crops benefitted on the weekend from rains in grain areas, traders said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The rains helped,&quot; one trader said. &quot;And the cooler temperatures help after all the heat we'd been having.&quot;</p>
<p>He added that soybeans in parts of Santa Fe and Cordoba provinces could still do with some more rain, but that generally crops were in good shape.</p>
<p>The Argentine Air Force's Meteorological Service forecast isolated showers in La Pampa, southwest Buenos Aires and northern Santa Fe for Monday.</p>
<p>Weather Services Corporation forecast highs of 79-93F (25-34C) in grain areas.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
